From 620f6260aa7eb8d7097eb30517688512f566fb21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:43:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Show every canvas of a session that started for stereo
 through a layer

The main window of a session that started with "Stereo 3D" on has an
alpha channel for the layer of a stereo canvas to show through, and
the surfaces that have alpha are 8 bits per channel here: Mesa has EGL
configs with alpha at 8, 10 and 16 bits (8/8/8/8, 10/10/10/2,
16/16/16/16 unorm and half float), but Qt Widgets takes the alpha size
of a top-level window to be 8 (translucent) or none, at the creation of
its QWidgetWindow, whatever the surface format says, so no deeper
window with alpha can be asked for from the application.

The canvases that are not a stereo pair would have dropped to the
8 bits of the window. They are shown through a layer too, with one
buffer and the canvas's own surface format, so that they keep the
depth of the canvas surface. A layer follows its canvas only while the
canvas is visible and not covered, which a canvas of a document in
another tab is not.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
